# ULX Styling Guidelines

## Paths
- **Style source**: `uls/node_modules/uls-v2`
- **Component source**: `src/components`

## ULX Styles
- **Primary**: `uls/node_modules/uls-v2/src/styles/uls-master.less`
- **Component styles**: `uls/node_modules/uls-v2/src/styles/uls-styles/less/`
  - `base/` - Variables, mixins, reset, utilities
  - `elements/` - Element components (button, input, etc.)
  - `collections/` - Collections (tabmenu, card, accordion, etc.)
  - `modules/` - Modules (dialog, table, etc.)
  - `themes/` - Theme files

## Rules
- **MUST** use existing ULX classes from `uls-styles/less/` for each component.
- **MUST** use the **ulx-** prefix and exact class names from those files (e.g. `.ulx-tabmenu`, `.ulx-button`, `.ulx-button-primary`, `.ulx-button-secondary`).
- **MUST** look up classes in the matching `.less` file under `uls/node_modules/uls-v2/src/styles/uls-styles/less/` before implementing.
- **NEVER** add custom CSS classes that duplicate ULX behavior.
- **NEVER** override ULX styles unless required; use `styles/uls/{app}/overrides/` and document why.
- **NEVER** use inline styles or component-specific CSS files for ULX look-and-feel.

## Example
```gjs
{{! ✅ CORRECT: ULX classes }}
<div class="ulx-tabmenu">
  <ul class="tabmenu-nav">
    <li class="tabmenu-item">
      <a class="tabmenu-link tabmenu-link-active">Tab 1</a>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>

{{! ❌ WRONG: Custom classes }}
<div class="my-custom-tabmenu">
  <ul class="my-nav">...</ul>
</div>
```

Styles come from `uls-master.less`; do not import styles in component files.
